# interplay_memlive_shared_subtree: Task 2's page table reaches into task 1's: task 1 is 2 deep, task 2 3 deep, and entry 1 of task 2's second-level table names task 1's last-level table for VA pages 4096-8191, so both tasks see the same leaves there (a walk reads whatever page an entry names, whatever table it came from). Task 2's first read of A and B at VA pages 4096 and 4097 waits on the gate while the guest rewrites the shared leaf of page 4097 and points task 1's own root entry 1 at a copy of the last-level table whose leaf for page 4096 names another page. Released, task 2 walks its own entry to the shared table: B is made over the rewritten leaf, and A over the unchanged one, not the copy's. Task 1 then walks the copy: its B (never made) is made over the copy's leaf, the old page.
